    {
      "id": 97627,
      "name": "ViolentSilence",
      "username": "ViolentSilence",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/v/bbe5ce/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2014-03-27T23:35:20.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>They do have more gamelines to support though, and I was thinking on the ride home about the unique difficulties of &gt;G. I'd guess what a lot of us respond to is the flavour of Sentinels, and part of why it works is that they're capturing a licenced product (in effect), even though no-one outside of Christopher and the creative team know the source material. They have to get the mechanics to be balanced, and yet capture the feel of his story. I don't see this being easier with three story lines to maintain! Even worse, is that it sounds like each expansion and core set for Sentinel Tactics will require Adam to produce a complete comic in addition to the artwork for the cards. Hopefully a core-set per year with an expansion between them will be possible, but it might not be that quick until after SotM reaches its conclusion</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:25:02.959Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
