      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>They do have more gamelines to support though, and I was thinking on the ride home about the unique difficulties of &gt;G. I&#39;d guess what a lot of us respond to is the flavour of Sentinels, and part of why it works is that they&#39;re capturing a licenced product (in effect), even though no-one outside of Christopher and the creative team know the source material. They have to get the mechanics to be balanced, and yet capture the feel of his story. I don&#39;t see this being easier with three story lines to maintain! Even worse, is that it sounds like each expansion and core set for Sentinel Tactics will require Adam to produce a complete comic in addition to the artwork for the cards. Hopefully a core-set per year with an expansion between them will be possible, but it might not be that quick until after SotM reaches its conclusion</p>",
